WEBVTT

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:04.880
<i>Today I'm having a studying 
session with Ao at my house!</i>

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.040
<i>But...</i>

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:08.050
The Johnson Comet...

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:10.780
Looks like it'll be going up 
to magnitude five this month.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:14.870
Five? Meaning we'll be able 
to see it with a telescope?

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:18.640
Yeah, I think we'll be able 
to see it with my telescope.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:23.630
There's also the Pan-STARRS comet, 
and the Tuttle-Giacobini-Kresák comet, too.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.670
That name's way too long.

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:31.300
Oh, that illustration...

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:32.330
This?

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.090
Nice, isn't it? I'm a fan of 
the person who drew this.

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:39.890
That's my mother's drawing.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:42.930
Huh? Your mother's an artist?

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.310
Yeah.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.150
She's what you'd call a science illustrator.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.370
Wow, that's incredible!

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.860
Hey, make-up test takers!

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.740
Oh, Suzu-chan.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:56.240
I'm glad I came to check on you.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.740
Stop slacking off and get to studying.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.480
<i>Reality is harsh.</i>

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:37.010
03. Memories Are Treasures

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:42.850
<i>Mira needs physics and English, 
and Ao's retaking math, huh?</i>

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:45.210
That's surprising.

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.600
Huh? What is?

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:50.220
You seem like you'd be 
good at the sciences, Ao.

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:54.820
<i>I can't tell her.</i>

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:59.280
<i>The star I saw the night before 
the test was so pretty,</i>

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:03.370
<i>I ended up writing its name 
instead of my own and got a 0.</i>

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:03.370
Manaka Antares

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:05.580
<i>I can't tell her that.</i>

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.910
Suzu-chan, help!

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:11.060
I don't understand this problem at all.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:12.420
Okay, okay.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:18.210
Let's see... For this problem, try using this 
formula to substitute for this value here.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:19.920
Oh, I see.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:22.440
Just be mindful of your units.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.280
Okay!

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:24.930
Thanks, Suzu-chan!

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:27.160
What?

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:33.190
Oh, um... I was just thinking you're 
awfully comfortable in Mira's house.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:36.120
Well, we've known each 
other for a long time.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.330
For example...

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:41.510
I know Mira keeps her sweet, pure,
self-made romance manga here.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.450
Wh-Why?!

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:47.190
Why not? It's pretty good.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.080
That's not the problem here!

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.000
You look confused.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:02.930
There are so many formulas, 
it's hard to memorize them all.

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:04.560
I see.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.930
At times like this, you should sing a song.

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:08.110
A song?

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:12.010
Yeah, make up a song about it, 
and you'll remember them easily.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:17.500
x=V0t+1/2at^2!

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:18.680
Ready, go!

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:25.140
x=V0t+1/2at^2!

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:30.990
V^2 - V0^2 = 2ax!

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:34.080
Doesn't adding a melody just create 
more you need to remember?

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:37.680
x=V0t+1/2at^2!

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:40.380
Oh, Onee-chan!

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:44.590
I thought I heard a strange song in here.
I see Suzu's stopped by.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.050
Misa-nee!

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:48.400
I brought some cream puffs
 and put them in the fridge!

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.560
Want to eat some?

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.500
Sure, I'll have some.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:54.210
I'll bring them right away!

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:57.150
Jeez, Suzu-chan's such a suck-up.

00:04:57.390 --> 00:05:01.120
Suzu-san seemed like a different
person for a moment there.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.000
She admires my older sister for some reason.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.070
Admires her?

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:09.330
Wh-What?

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:12.910
Y-Y-Your face was too close!

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:16.670
I haven't seen you before.

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:19.640
Oh, n-nice to meet you.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:23.170
I'm a first-year in the earth sciences club. 
My name is Manaka Ao.

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:24.850
Oh, I get it.

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:27.200
So you're Ao-kun. Nice to meet you.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:28.100
Huh?

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.890
I've heard about you from Mira.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:33.600
Also, while your hair is different, 
you look kind of similar...

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:37.570
to the main character in the 
romance manga Mira drew.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:38.980
You've seen it, too?!

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:41.440
I'd love to read it, too.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:43.610
No! Absolutely not!

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:45.400
You're the one person who can never read it!

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:52.700
Wh-What is it?

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:58.300
You're not reacting the 
same way when I do it.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:59.040
That's interesting.

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:04.670
Suzu-chan, the cream puffs!

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:08.840
Thank goodness. They're not crushed.

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:12.500
They're good!

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:15.310
That's Suzuya Bakery's cream puffs for you!

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.820
Suzu, what are you upset about?

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.570
I'm not upset.

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:22.840
I don't care what you happen to think of Ao.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:25.890
Don't get the wrong idea about me.

00:06:25.890 --> 00:06:27.740
I was conducting an experiment.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:29.490
So Ao-kun is...

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:31.110
a guinea pig.

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:32.370
A guinea pig?

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:34.630
Ugh! Cut it out, Onee-chan!

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:36.580
Stop saying weird things to Ao!

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:37.740
Sorry.

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:39.890
That's being rude to your friend, isn't it?

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:41.130
That's right!

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:43.700
Ao's my precious partner!

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:44.800
Partner?

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:46.920
Huh? Haven't you heard, Misa-nee?

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:48.680
They're looking for an aster—

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.340
Ah, Suzu-chan!

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:51.680
Keep that a secret from my sister, okay?

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:54.740
I want to find it on my own.

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:58.540
Correction!

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:01.890
They're partners in trying to raise 
an elementary school girl.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.520
What the heck? That's so random!

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:05.380
Huh? You think so?

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:08.070
I thought it was pretty clever, personally.

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.200
Anyway...

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:13.560
Sorry for interrupting.

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.660
I'll be studying in my room, too.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:16.790
For a test?

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.850
No, for entrance exams.

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:21.920
I want to have fun during the summer,
 so I need to get ahead now.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.500
Oh, right, Onee-chan.

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:25.960
Here, you can have this.

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:27.740
It's a banded stone!

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:29.300
We found one during club.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:32.760
They're considered lucky, 
so I hope it helps with your exams.

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:37.350
Thanks.

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:40.760
I'm glad to see you're enjoying your club.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:44.220
Ao-kun, please take good 
care of my little sister.

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:46.150
Okay.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.280
Pocket 
Astronomy

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.280
<b>Encyclopedia 
of Star Names</b>

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:53.320
Misa-neesan's so cool.

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:54.660
I was so nervous.

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:56.200
Right?

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:59.420
I can't believe she's already 
studying for her entrance exams.

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:03.960
Entrance exams?

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:08.880
There.

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:11.090
That should do it.

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:16.260
Still, an asteroid, huh?

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:18.390
Mira's set a big dream for herself.

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:20.850
Please take care of them both.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:22.690
The noises stopped.

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:26.440
I can't get enough of 
Misa-nee's mysterious nature!

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:32.670
<i>After all that, both Ao and 
I passed our make-up exams.</i>

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:38.160
Penniless Squad Broke Rangers!

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:41.720
Say something already!

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:45.500
Huh? Oh... You can't be 
a sentai team by yourself.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.340
Yes, yes, my new part-time pretties.

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:51.070
Hurry up and change into your battle uniforms.

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:56.430
<i>Today I'm here, working part-time 
with Ao at the Suzuya Bakery!</i>

00:08:57.380 --> 00:09:00.220
Ao, are you embarrassed?

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:03.140
Yeah. I've never worn an 
outfit like this before.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:07.320
Suzu-chan, it's so frilly and hard to move in!

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:09.390
Can I tuck the back up?

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:11.440
You should be a bit more embarrassed, Mira.

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:16.950
Okay. Mira-chan, Ao-san, 
we're counting on you today.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:17.840
Sure.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:19.310
It's a pleasure to work with you.

00:09:19.310 --> 00:09:22.660
Can you get started by setting 
this bread out in the store?

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:24.910
Wow, a hexagon!

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:28.440
Columnar jointing!

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:30.590
Just set them out like normal!

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:35.300
It's about time to open the store!

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:37.740
I-I'm getting nervous.

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:40.840
Don't worry. I'll be here 
with you. Just calm down.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:42.010
Suzu-chan...

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:45.850
Good morning!

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:48.560
What should I get?

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:51.820
Mommy, I want this Fairy's Ocarina.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:56.450
Their newest product, the English Maid's 
Morning, looks very delicious.

00:09:57.060 --> 00:09:59.540
That's some unique naming sense.

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:01.740
It's a little embarrassing.

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:03.830
Oh, part-timers?

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:06.370
So many people!

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:09.080
Next is, uh...

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:09.080
S-Suzu-chan!

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:11.260
Moe-Moe, you're so cute today!

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:13.910
Oh, my. You're always so nice.

00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:13.910
Hey!

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:16.800
Suzu-chan, you said you 
were going to stay with us!

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:19.760
Noblewoman's 
Tea Party

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:22.300
Here's 20 yen in change and your receipt.

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:24.260
Here's your order!

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:26.930
Thank you very much!

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:31.140
You two are getting the hang of it quick.

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:34.840
Thanks to your spartan training 
of leaving us on our own.

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:37.690
Speaking of spartan, can I 
request one more thing from you?

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:41.440
When you're in front of customers,
 remember to smile!

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:45.020
Welco—

00:10:45.020 --> 00:10:47.560
Oh, Megu, welcome back.

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:48.500
Thanks.

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:52.830
Huh? Megu-chan?! It's been so... long...

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:56.460
I-I mistook you for someone else.

00:10:56.900 --> 00:11:00.470
No, um, you're right. I'm Megu.

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:02.040
Megu-san?

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:03.720
My little sister.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:06.680
She's really grown taller 
since she joined her club.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:09.180
She got taller than me 
in the blink of an eye.

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:12.100
Mira-chan, it's good to see you again.

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:13.870
Nice to meet you, Ao-san.

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:16.240
I'll go get ready.

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:26.280
Uh, my sister said this 
outfit would go over better...

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:29.870
I think that's some nice coordination, 
if I do say so myself!

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:32.080
Thank you for always coming by.

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:35.340
Have a sample.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:38.670
B-Be careful.

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:41.500
What's wrong, Mira?

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:44.600
The only thing I can do is 
stack bread up neatly.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:46.430
Wow!

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:53.120
Um, Ao-san, does my sister 
have fun at school?

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:58.960
Since I'm busy with my club, she has 
to help with the store more often.

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:01.650
I was wondering if she was still 
getting along well with everyone.

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:10.070
I think she's fine. She's having lots of fun.

00:12:10.070 --> 00:12:11.370
Why the pause, then?

00:12:11.590 --> 00:12:13.030
Oh, uh...

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:17.240
She's not a member of the earth sciences club, 
so I don't get to spend much time with her.

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:20.380
But she does watch over us 
from the perfect distance,

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:23.630
so she's kind of like an 
older sister to us, too.

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:25.690
I-I see.

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:27.060
That's good.

00:12:27.060 --> 00:12:29.350
Wow. An older sister, huh?

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:33.350
You can be my little sister 
starting today if you want!

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:38.730
I'm beat.

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:41.040
It was fun, though.

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:43.240
Yeah! I want to do it again!

00:12:44.140 --> 00:12:46.000
Thanks for your help.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:47.700
Here, take this with you.

00:12:48.340 --> 00:12:52.440
Did you know the word "croissant" 
means "crescent moon"?

00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:56.280
Huh? It's a bit thick for a crescent moon.

00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:58.200
This is more like a waxing crescent.

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:01.300
Jeez, you two really 
know how to ruin things!

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:03.550
Here, your pay for today.

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:06.380
Thanks for your work today.

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:07.660
I hope we can count on you again.

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:09.260
Thank you very much!

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:11.870
Our first part-time paychecks...

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:14.100
Huh? Isn't this a lot?

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:15.710
Non, non.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:21.070
I got to take lots of photos, 
so I added extra as your modeling fee.

00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:24.260
I-I'm sorry! I'm sorry about my sister!

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:26.990
I learned these secret photo 
tricks from Monroe-senpai!

00:13:24.260 --> 00:13:25.520
Oh, it's fine.

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:26.990
We're used to it.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:39.300
<i>The maps I received from my 
friend when I was little</i>

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:41.040
Animal Pen

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:41.040
School 
Building

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:41.040
Pond

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:43.210
<i>were genuine treasure maps in my mind.</i>

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.760
Towel, sunscreen...

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:49.050
Okay, all set.

00:13:50.060 --> 00:13:51.850
I'm heading out.

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:57.350
There you are!

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:58.580
Ao!

00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:00.200
Did I keep you waiting?

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:02.440
No, I just got here.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:04.980
I see. That's good.

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:08.250
Oh, that sounded like what people 
on a date would say, didn't it?

00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:10.070
A d-date?

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:13.920
Well, let's get started with "Shopping to 
Commemorate Our First Part-Time Paychecks,"

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:16.540
also known as our "Station Area Date"!

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:22.730
Today I want to go to the stationery store, 
the bookstore, and...

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:24.420
Mira, look.

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:28.710
Ino-senpai and... Suzu-chan?

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:32.010
When did those two get so close?

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:35.270
Let's follow them for a bit!

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:36.930
Huh? Uh, okay...

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:44.910
It doesn't look like they're out shopping.

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:47.400
Oh, they went into a residential area.

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:56.830
Ino-senpai looks kind of happy.

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:59.660
"Senpai's photographing something nao."

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:05.880
Ino-senpai's opening up... a map?

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:08.920
"Senpai's opening up a map nao."

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:15.500
Oh, they went into an alley.

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:17.890
"They went into an alley nao."

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:22.070
I wonder where they're going, though.

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:23.720
"We don't know their destination—"

00:15:23.720 --> 00:15:24.540
Hey!

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:29.630
What a coincidence.

00:15:29.630 --> 00:15:30.610
Hey.

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:33.380
I'm sorry we followed you.

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:35.080
We got caught nao.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:37.520
Enough of the "nao" stuff already.

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:40.190
Mira-chan, Ao-san, good afternoon.

00:15:40.190 --> 00:15:43.900
What were you doing in a 
place like this? On a date?

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:46.920
Oh, no, nothing like that!

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:48.170
You sound happy, though.

00:15:48.620 --> 00:15:53.360
I wanted to come see the enclave today, 
so I asked Suzu-san to accompany me.

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:54.390
Enclave?

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:59.600
Yes! It's a part of a territory that lies 
within another territory, like this.

00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:02.530
Huh. Is that interesting?

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:03.980
Yes, it is!

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:08.810
I've always loved maps, so every 
now and then, I go exploring like this.

00:16:08.810 --> 00:16:10.200
That sounds fun.

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:13.350
Were maps something the 
geology group studied, too?

00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:15.920
They're probably considered 
a slightly different field,

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:18.330
but they're pretty closely related.

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:23.000
Last year, we found a cute map 
in front the geology club room.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:24.760
Colorful and pretty, isn't it?

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:27.960
It's a geological map.

00:16:28.350 --> 00:16:30.670
It was a meeting with destiny.

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:35.380
That was what made me join the club,

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:39.070
so it's only rather recently that I've 
taken an interest in geology and stones.

00:16:39.070 --> 00:16:42.560
Wow. There are all kinds of 
ways to get into it, huh?

00:16:42.870 --> 00:16:44.140
Senpai!

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:46.730
I found our landmark!

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:49.190
Kinuichi
Kawanishi 
2-Chome

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:49.190
There! That's it, right?

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:52.300
Oh, that's the district signboard!

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:53.730
Selfie, selfie!

00:16:53.730 --> 00:16:55.580
I have to make a record of this!

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:00.110
Ino-senpai!

00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:02.370
Okay, one more!

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:11.920
Whew, we really walked a lot.

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:16.890
Ino-senpai, you should just do things 
like we did today during our club time.

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:19.720
We could join you for it, too.

00:17:19.940 --> 00:17:22.670
No, this is my hobby.

00:17:22.670 --> 00:17:25.980
I figure it's good to draw a line 
between hobbies and club activities.

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:28.860
I'd just be bothering Sakura-senpai, anyway.

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:30.630
So mature.

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:34.490
Senpai... what made you love maps?

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:37.570
Oh, I want to hear this, too!

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:43.480
It was probably the treasure maps 
my friend often drew for me long ago.

00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:46.880
I had so much fun going out 
with them and exploring.

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:48.880
How charming!

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:51.100
What were the treasures?

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:55.840
Praying mantis eggs, a beehive, 
some dirty magazines someone threw out...

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:01.790
Searching for the treasure was fun,

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:05.980
but walking around with the map

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:09.710
made the parks and roads I always 
used seem completely different.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:13.860
So many flowers!

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:21.280
I lost track of that friend after we ended up 
going to different middle schools, though.

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:25.320
I want to try treasure hunting, too!

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:28.060
Ino-senpai, would you draw us a map?!

00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:30.110
Huh? I don't mind, but...

00:18:30.110 --> 00:18:31.500
We don't have any paper.

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:35.050
Oh, I know! Draw it on my hand!

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:36.390
Your hand?!

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:38.880
P-Please give me some time.

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:40.760
I'll draw a proper one.

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:43.860
We should get going.

00:18:43.860 --> 00:18:46.520
I'll cover the bill as thanks for today.

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:47.980
So mature!

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:53.740
This might be my first time 
drawing a map myself.

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:59.320
<b>Ino</b>

00:18:57.840 --> 00:18:59.320
<i>H-Hello?</i>

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:02.250
Oh, Ino, do you have a moment?

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:03.310
<i>Yes!</i>

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:05.660
Thanks for sending me that picture.

00:19:06.150 --> 00:19:09.540
<i>I just happened to find some 
stones that share your name,</i>

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:11.990
and it made me happy, so I sent it.

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:15.550
<i>I already made it my wallpaper.</i>

00:19:19.430 --> 00:19:21.720
<i>Ino? What's the matter?</i>

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:24.060
Huh? Oh.

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:28.310
Senpai, um...

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:29.100
<i>Hmm?</i>

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:35.060
I ended up agreeing to draw a treasure 
map for Mira-chan and the others,

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:37.940
but I was wondering what kind 
of map they might enjoy.

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:42.290
I see. You're sharing your fun with them.

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:44.160
<i>Sharing my fun?</i>

00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:47.820
<i>Whatever you find fun is the treasure.</i>

00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:52.100
<i>If you draw a map to that, 
I'm sure those girls will love it.</i>

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:55.300
Okay!

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:58.500
<b>Class 1-1</b>

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:01.590
Mira-chan, sorry to make you wait for it.

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:02.590
Here you go.

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:05.710
Wow! Thank you so much!

00:20:05.710 --> 00:20:09.560
I wonder what Ino-senpai's 
treasure is. I can't wait!

00:20:10.840 --> 00:20:13.820
Please try to find it together after school.

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:14.770
Okay!

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:23.110
Now, after Ino-senpai's treasure!

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:24.780
Let's go!

00:20:25.110 --> 00:20:29.490
Let's see... First we go through this passage 
and head toward the special classroom wing.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:35.830
The anatomical model here is scary, so run!

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:43.770
It says here, "The koi in the courtyard's 
pond are cute. Photo spot."

00:20:43.770 --> 00:20:47.850
It's fun learning what 
Ino-senpai usually sees.

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:52.230
I didn't know you could enjoy maps this way.

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:54.560
<b>Earth Sciences Lab</b>

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:59.210
The final landmark is... 
"The back of a cute map."

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:01.380
This one!

00:21:01.380 --> 00:21:03.740
It really is colorful and cute.

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:07.870
Oh, there's something on the back.

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:11.490
A letter and... the photo from yesterday!

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:14.410
Ino-senpai's so cute!

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:16.450
Too cute!

00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:18.670
Gosh...

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:20.530
Ino-senpai!

00:21:21.820 --> 00:21:23.840
We found the treasure!

00:21:24.270 --> 00:21:26.510
It was fun hunting for treasure.

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:28.550
Please draw another map again sometime!

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:30.840
Sure, I'd love to!

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:38.880
<i>This was how I managed to share the 
fun I had with those treasure maps</i>

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:41.330
<i>I received back then with everyone here.</i>

00:21:42.040 --> 00:21:48.500
<i>I hope I can share this fun 
with more and more people.</i>

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:51.930
Summer camp?

00:21:51.930 --> 00:21:55.040
Yeah. You haven't decided 
where to go yet, right?

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:56.750
I have a nice idea of my own.

00:21:57.300 --> 00:21:58.960
A nice idea?

00:22:00.280 --> 00:22:03.980
<i>It sounds like the earth sciences club 
is about to get even more exciting!</i>

00:23:34.990 --> 00:23:40.000
04.
Exciting! Summer Camp!

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:39.350
Next time, "Exciting! Summer Camp!"
